# Tessera stdlib: the ThreadLocalManager, the `@threadlocal` globals of a program's threads

module Standard/System/Memory

### The manager of the program's thread-locals: the block of `@threadlocal` globals each thread has. With an
### operating system, it makes a thread's block, every global at its starting value, when the thread starts, and takes
### it back when the thread ends. On AArch64 without one, the link script holds the block of the flow the reset starts
### (prepare_core puts the globals at their starting values there), and a ThreadManagerByRoundRobin holds one in each
### thread's slot. Its routines are called on the type.
entity ThreadLocalManager
    nothing

### Makes the manager. It holds no values.
### :returns: The manager.
common routine ThreadLocalManager.construct() -> Me
    return Me()

### Puts every `@threadlocal` global of the program back to its starting value on this thread: a thread worker does it
### before each ticket's work.
common routine ThreadLocalManager.reset() -> None
    reset_all_thread_locals()
    return

### Stores every `@threadlocal` global's starting value into this thread's block (the builder writes the routine).
@external("llvm")
@template("call void @tessera.reset_thread_locals()")
secret routine reset_all_thread_locals() -> None
